      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T07:18:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at your first comment again I don\u0027t think you should see that neither ConnectivityManager nor RoutingCoordinatorManager can import IRoutingCoordinator; actually I would expect ConnectivityManager to be able to import IRoutingCoordinator fine, since it\u0027s in the sources just as IConnectivityManager.\n\nSo I think the missing piece was that connectivity-internal-api-util didn\u0027t see hidden, non-unsupportedappusage classes of framework-connectivity. So after making the change, a comment explaining that connectivity-internal-api-util depends on framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar and framework-connectivity-tiramisu-pre-jarjar so that it has access to all hidden classes, as opposed to framework-connectivity.impl which only allows reliably importing API classes, would probably be useful ? You can probably advise better on what kind of information would have been useful to unblock you yesterday though.\n\nGenerally when getting this kind of \"can\u0027t find class X\" errors, as a last resort it\u0027s helpful to find the lib that you expect contains the class in the out/ directory, and unzip it to see if the class is there. You\u0027d see it\u0027s jarjared, and then you\u0027re a bit closer to the answer. I\u0027ll put some doc on the team site for advice around that.",
